# One byte sequence per file, on every machine that checks this tree out.
#
# `schema/crucible-code-schema.json` is generated and compared against what is
# checked in, byte for byte, so that the file cannot drift from the declaration
# it comes from. A Windows checkout with the usual `core.autocrlf` rewrites the
# checked-in copy on the way to disk, which makes that comparison fail for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the schema. `scripts/*.sh` would be handed
# to a shell with carriage returns in it for the same reason.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than plain `text=auto`: the working tree is what those two
# read, not the blob.
* text=auto eol=lf
